From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] linux 7.2: sync the addr shadow after registration

The pre-register dev_addr write cannot update dev_addr_shadow because
the netdev address list is not initialized yet. Sync it right after a
successful register, before the interface can be opened.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/os_dep/linux/os_intfs.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/os_intfs.c
@@ -2303,6 +2303,11 @@
 	else
 		ret = (register_netdevice(ndev) == 0) ? _SUCCESS : _FAIL;
 
+	/* The address list exists now; sync the shadow the pre-register
+	 * write could not update. */
+	if (ret == _SUCCESS)
+		rtw_set_netdev_addr(ndev, adapter_mac_addr(adapter));
+
 	if (ret == _SUCCESS)
 		adapter->registered = 1;
 	else
